BFS depth limit off-by-one: when a node at `maxDepth` is dequeued, edges are explored and the target can be discovered and returned without checking the depth constraint. The path will have `maxDepth + 1` edges, exceeding the configured limit. Specifically, at line 256 the `depth + 1 > maxDepth` guard only gates *further exploration* (enqueue), but the early-return at line 257-259 for the target bypasses it.

Scenario: `maxDepth=2`, graph `A→B→C→D`, call `path(A, D)`. Node C is dequeued at depth 2, edge C→D is processed, target is found, and a 3-edge path `[A→B, B→C, C→D]` is returned.

Fix: check `depth + 1 > maxDepth` before accepting the target:
```typescript
if (e.dst_canonical === to) {
  if (depth + 1 > maxDepth) continue;
  if (!cameFrom.has(to)) cameFrom.set(to, { prev: node, edge: e });
  return buildPath(to);
}
```

