`buildTemporalFilter` is called twice in `temporal()` with the identical `filter` argument, producing identical clauses and params for both the node and edge queries. Since both tables have the same column names for temporal filtering, the result could be computed once and reused:
```typescript
const temporalFilter = buildTemporalFilter(filter);
nodeSql += temporalFilter.clauses;
nodeParams.push(...temporalFilter.params);
// ...
edgeSql += temporalFilter.clauses;
edgeParams.push(...temporalFilter.params);
```
This avoids redundant validation + string concatenation. Minor, but the pattern of calling a pure function twice with the same input suggests the intermediate result should be hoisted.

